  "body": "Printing a page involves creating/displaying a modal dialog which is not desirable during navigations and can cause several issues.\r\n\r\nCurrently, Firefox already ignores print() during the unload handlers, and Chrome is broken in several cases (see https://groups.google.com/a/chromium.org/d/msg/blink-dev/sBE6zziflmQ/5eiD0yh7BAAJ). Edge also has problems when trying to print from unload handlers.\r\n\r\nThe current spec allows the browser to abort printing at any time:\r\n* https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#printing\r\n\r\nShould the spec explicitly disallow printing in the unload handlers, so that this is interoperable?\r\n",
